# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, whatever core.autocrlf
# says: Prettier (run through ESLint) formats with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The World Editor owns every file of a map folder (a folder named *.w3m or
# *.w3x, anywhere); git stores them byte for byte, whatever core.autocrlf says.
**/*.w3m/** -text
**/*.w3x/** -text

# Its Object data files are binary: reforged-map's textconv driver shows them
# to git diff as text, one line per object and per modification. pnpm install
# sets the driver's command in the clone's git configuration
# (scripts/diff-driver.ts). war3map.wts and war3map.lua diff as text already.
**/*.w3m/war3map.w3[utahbdq] diff=reforged-object-data
**/*.w3m/war3mapSkin.w3[utahbdq] diff=reforged-object-data
**/*.w3x/war3map.w3[utahbdq] diff=reforged-object-data
**/*.w3x/war3mapSkin.w3[utahbdq] diff=reforged-object-data

# The pipeline tests' fixture map is a copy of those editor-saved files: its
# bytes (the war3map.w3i hash, the war3map.lua text) are what the tests pin.
# The provenance note beside them (objects-map.md) is text, as every file.
tests/pipeline/fixtures/*.w3m/** -text -diff

# template-maintenance:start
# The lock of the Upstream skills, part of the copy of what the library
# shares: git stores it byte for byte, as .claude/.gitattributes does the
# rest of the copy (.claude/shared.lock.json records each file's sha256).
# Template maintenance: pnpm template:detach removes this block.
skills-lock.json -text
# template-maintenance:end
